  "functions": [
    "FUNC.DATEDIF"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "DATEDIF unit \"MD\" can return negative day counts when crossing a shorter preceding month",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, DATEDIF(start_date, end_date, unit) truncates both serials, rejects start_date > end_date or unknown unit strings (anything outside trimmed case-insensitive Y, M, D, YM, YD, MD) with #NUM!, and for unit \"MD\" when end_day < start_day computes end_day + days_in_previous_month(end_year, end_month) - start_day. When start_day exceeds the month preceding end_date (e.g. 2001-01-31 to 2001-03-01, crossing 28-day February), \"MD\" returns -2 (and 2001-01-30 to 2001-03-01 returns -1). All 2,914 full-bank DATEDIF rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (jnt_dates_random rows 65-75 and f2_rows rows 133-137); 2,914/2,914 full-bank rows match.",
  "inferred": null,
  "documentation": null,
